  "notes": "v163: P&L tells the whole truth now. Driver wages are a fixed line of their own in your expenses — always there, figured by the app, never typed — and a connected driver's wages price at HIS OWN rate, the wage he set on his own side (you never set a driver's wage; the old set-his-pay door is gone). Monthly miles come only from the truck's odometer — the miles text box is gone. The NATL line is deleted, and a + at the end of the expense lines adds your own custom lines. Maintenance: the 'between fill-ups' line is deleted, and lifetime distance is the odometer bookend figure, hardened so a bad reading can never bend it. Preferences: the pay card now says Driver wage rate.",
